IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Ontario Works -- the dates of the internal review and appeal time limits (O. Reg. 134/98 ss 69 (1), 72 (1), (2)), kept in
-- their own module so that only it and the seat import daydate.
-- © King's Printer for Ontario, 1998. NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION (see on-ow.l4 and SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Ontario Works -- review and appeal dates`

-- s 69 (1): "30 days from the day the decision is received or deemed to have been received". The last day is read as the
-- day 30 days after receipt.
GIVEN `the day the decision was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to request an internal review` MEANS `the day the decision was received` PLUS 30

-- s 72 (1): "30 days from the day the administrator's decision is final under clause 25 (3) (b) of the Act"; (2): "No
-- appeal to the Tribunal shall be commenced more than one year after the date of the administrator's decision." The
-- earlier of the two.
GIVEN `the day the decision became final` IS A DATE, `the date of the administrator's decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to appeal to the Tribunal` MEANS
    LET `thirty days` MEANS `the day the decision became final` PLUS 30
        `one year` MEANS `add years` `the date of the administrator's decision` 1
    IN  IF `thirty days` AT MOST `one year` THEN `thirty days` ELSE `one year`
